   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Was y were",
   "texto": [
    "El pasado de «to be» tiene dos formas. **Was** va con I, he, she, it: **I was at home** (estaba en casa). **Were** va con you, we, they: **They were at work**.",
    "Negación: **wasn't** y **weren't**. Pregunta: **Were you at home?** — **Yes, I was** / **No, I wasn't**.",
    "Para nacer se usa siempre el pasado: **I was born in Madrid** (nací en Madrid)."
   ]
